# The QTI system helper ships with <application android:enabled="false">, so its
# systemhelperaidl services (ISystemTUICallback and friends) never register and
# mitrustedui keeps asking servicemanager to lazy-start them. Enable it once boot
# has completed; the package manager keeps the setting from then on.
on property:sys.boot_completed=1
    exec_background u:r:shell:s0 shell shell -- /system/bin/sh -c "cmd package enable com.qualcomm.qti.services.systemhelper"
